idekerno: Linux kernel version 1.1.18, without SCSI support.
idekerno: 
idekerno: A Linux kernel for computers that do not need SCSI support. If you 
idekerno: don't have SCSI, the advantage of using the idekern kernel is that 
idekerno: your machine will boot faster with a leaner kernel. See the file
idekerno: 'idekern.log' for an exact list of included drivers. A short list:
idekerno:  
idekerno: This kernel also has support for PPP, UMSDOS, CSLIP, ethernet,
idekerno: Ftape, and the PS/2 style mouse (but not other busmouse types).
